 "intro_html": "Japanese rice balls. The rice is <b>plain</b> short-grain rice, seasoned only by the salt on your hands — not <a href=\"sushi-rice.html\">sushi rice</a>, which is vinegared and too soft and sharp for this. Shape them <b>by hand</b> (left hand underneath, right hand the roof) or <b>with a mold</b>; fill them with the classics or something louder; hide a whole marinated egg in a <b>bakudan</b> (“bomb”); or grill them into <b>yaki onigiri</b>.",
