   "part_id": "part-fillings",
   "time": "~6 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~6 min</span>",
   "title": "Loud fillings",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\">1–2 tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Sriracha (spicy tuna-mayo)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"3\" data-b=\"4\" data-f=\"piece|pieces\" data-n=\"3\">3–4 pieces</span>",
     "name_html": "Karaage, leftover"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"60\">60 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Kimchi, chopped and squeezed"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"40\">40 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Cheese (mozzarella or cheddar), small cubes"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Let the rice cool just until you can hold it — it must still be warm to stick.</li><li>Wet both palms with a little water.</li><li>Dip 2–3 fingers in kosher salt and rub it over both palms (table salt: half as much).</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Wet and salt your hands",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Wet both palms, then dip 2–3 fingers in kosher salt…",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/5-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "…and rub the salt over both palms.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/5-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/5.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": "Shape by hand",
   "part_id": "part-shape-by-hand",
   "time": "~5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min</span>",
   "title": "Wet and salt your hands",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "a little for each onigiri",
     "name_html": "Kosher salt (for your hands)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Scoop ~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"50\" data-s=\"0\">50 g</span> warm rice onto your LEFT palm — the left hand always stays underneath.</li><li>Press a small well in the middle and put in <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">1–2 tsp</span> of one filling.</li><li>Cover with another ~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"50\" data-s=\"0\">50 g</span> of rice and press it gently round the filling into a ball.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-6",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Rice, filling, close",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "About 50 g of warm rice on your left palm; press a small well into the middle.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/6-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "1–2 tsp of filling in the well, then cover with more rice.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/6-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/6.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 6,
   "part": "Shape by hand",
   "part_id": "part-shape-by-hand",
   "time": "1 min each",
   "time_html": "<span>1 min each</span>",
   "title": "Rice, filling, close",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>RIGHT hand on top, fingers together and bent into a roof — it makes the corner.</li><li>LEFT hand underneath in a “C” — fingers and heel gently flatten the two sides.</li><li>Press lightly, then roll the corner you just made <b>towards you</b> — a third of a turn.</li><li>Three corners, then 2–3 more rounds. Lay it on each face and press once to flatten.</li><li>Firm enough to hold together, but airy inside — don’t squeeze.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-7",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Press the triangle",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Right hand on top, fingers together and bent like a roof; left hand underneath in a “C”, pressing the sides.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/7-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Press lightly, then roll the corner you just made towards you — a third of a turn — and press again.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/7-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/7.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 7,
   "part": "Shape by hand",
   "part_id": "part-shape-by-hand",
   "time": "~1 min each",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 min each</span>",
   "title": "Press the triangle",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Line a small bowl with plastic wrap and sprinkle in a little salt.</li><li>Rice in, a well, the filling, more rice on top, a little more salt.</li><li>Gather and twist the wrap shut, then press the same triangle through it. Good for lunchboxes — nobody’s hands touch the rice.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-8",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Or: through plastic wrap",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Rice and filling on plastic wrap in a bowl; gather and twist it shut, then press the triangle.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/8-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/8.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 8,
   "part": "Shape by hand",
   "part_id": "part-shape-by-hand",
   "time": "~1 min each",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 min each</span>",
   "title": "Or: through plastic wrap",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Dip the mold and its lid in water, shake off the excess, and sprinkle salt inside.</li><li>Fill it halfway with warm rice, pushing it into the corners.</li><li>A spoonful of filling in the middle, then rice to the brim and a little salt on top.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-9",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Fill the mold",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Fill the wet mold halfway, pushing the rice into the corners.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/9-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Filling in the middle, then rice to the brim.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/9-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/9.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 9,
   "part": "Shape with a mold",
   "part_id": "part-shape-with-a-mold",
   "time": "~1 min each",
   "time_html": "<span>~1 min each</span>",
   "title": "Fill the mold",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Lid on and push down firmly — you should feel a slight resistance. No resistance? Add a little rice.</li><li>Lid off, flip the mold over the tray and push the button to pop the onigiri out.</li><li>Wet your fingers before touching it. A mold makes smaller, denser onigiri (~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"75\" data-s=\"0\">75 g</span> each, 13 from the pot); a lighter push keeps them fluffier.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-10",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Press and push out",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Lid on and press down firmly — stop when you feel resistance.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/10-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Flip it over and push the button to pop the onigiri out.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/10-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/10.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 10,
   "part": "Shape with a mold",
   "part_id": "part-shape-with-a-mold",
   "time": "~30 s each",
   "time_html": "<span>~30 s each</span>",
   "title": "Press and push out",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Take the eggs out of the marinade and stir <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"0.25\" data-s=\"0\">¼ cup</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"60\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">60 ml</span>)</span> of it into ~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"600\" data-s=\"0\">600 g</span> of the warm rice.</li><li>~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"150\" data-s=\"0\">150 g</span> of that rice in your left palm, a well in the middle, one whole egg in it.</li><li>Cover with more rice and shape it round, the egg in the centre.</li><li>Wrap it all over in a whole nori sheet — the black ball is the bomb.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-11",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Bakudan — the bomb",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "About 150 g of seasoned rice in your palm, a whole marinated egg in the middle.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/11-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Cover it, shape a round ball, then wrap it all over in a whole sheet of nori.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/11-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/11.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 11,
   "part": "Bakudan",
   "part_id": "part-bakudan",
   "time": "~2 min each",
   "time_html": "<span>~2 min each</span>",
   "title": "Bakudan — the bomb",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"3\" data-f=\"sheet|sheets\" data-n=\"1\">3 sheets</span>",
     "name_html": "Nori"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wrap a third of a nori sheet round the bottom of each onigiri — <b>right before eating</b> for crisp nori, or now for soft nori that sticks.</li><li>Or skip the nori: coat the three faces in <a href=\"furikake.html\">furikake</a> with wet fingers.</li><li>A little of the filling on the tip tells you what’s inside. Eat warm or at room temperature, within about 6 hours.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-12",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Nori, furikake, a dab on top",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Wrap a third of a nori sheet round the bottom just before eating — the nori stays crisp.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/12-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Or coat the faces in furikake with damp fingers.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/12-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/12.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 12,
   "part": "Finish",
   "part_id": "part-finish",
   "time": "~4 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~4 min</span>",
   "title": "Nori, furikake, a dab on top",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "to coat (optional)",
     "name_html": "Furikake"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Press plain onigiri a bit firmer than usual so they don’t break in the pan.</li><li>Parchment in a frying pan, onigiri on it, medium-low heat.</li><li>Leave each side until crisp and lightly browned before turning (two spatulas) — handling them too early breaks them.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-low",
    "label_html": "<span>medium-low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-13",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Yaki onigiri: grill",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Turn each one only when its side is crisp, with two spatulas.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigiri/13-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigiri/13.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 13,
   "part": "Yaki onigiri",
   "part_id": "part-yaki-onigiri",
   "time": "~10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~10 min</span>",
   "title": "Yaki onigiri: grill",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Heat to low. Brush one side with the soy sauce and sesame oil, turn it onto the pan, brush the other.</li><li>A minute more per side — the glaze burns fast.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "low",
    "label_html": "<span>low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-14",
   "images": {
